-- title:
--   Conjugate Gauss rings unramified over Γ₀(M'): case q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing an element $\zeta$ that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), the field generated by ratios $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with $H = \ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times\big)$; and let $K_0$ be the analogous base change of the $q$-expansion field of $\Gamma_0(M')$, assumed to satisfy $K_0 \le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f\cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and let $O_0 \subseteq K_0$ be characterised by the same condition. Let $\tau$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ and assume that an element of $K_0$ lies in $O_0$ precisely when its image in $K$ lies in $\tau^{-1}(W_0)$, so that $B := \tau^{-1}(W_0)$ is an $O_0$-algebra. Then the ramification index of the maximal ideal of $B$ over the maximal ideal of $O_0$ equals $1$.
--
--   This is the statement that every conjugate, by an $L$-automorphism of the level field, of the Gauss (Igusa) valuation ring at the cusp $\infty$ is unramified over the corresponding Gauss ring of the base field of $\Gamma_0(M')$, in the case $q=3$, where the relevant Igusa covering of the $\infty$-branch is degenerate. It feeds the combined statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_comap_eq_and_ramificationIdx_eq_one_and_isSeparable_of_over_gauss_gamma0_mul_xH_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_comap_eq_and_ramificationIdx_eq_one_and_isSeparable_of_over_gauss_gamma0_mul_xH_of_eq_three), which packages the lying-over, ramification-index-one and separability assertions used in the semistability analysis of the modular curve at level $q^2M'$.
